on of Mecca for prayer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7404-8daa-d5d553a1b6ae","description":"Mosque","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-732f-a7a4-d8ae39027f3f","description":"Church","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7373-a457-ded3836a8d5b","description":"Synagogue","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7f8a-be04-dce385de1e5b","description":"Temple","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-79fd-ad71-6579fc2f52a2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who co-founded Apple with Steve Wozniak?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Steve Jobs left Apple in 1985 and founded NeXT; Apple later bought NeXT, bringing him back to the company.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7a57-b060-93167d8e8ec9","description":"Steve Jobs","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7e52-9d70-2928fbe080bb","description":"Bill Gates","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-714a-a2ec-c29eb43887e3","description":"Thomas Watson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-782e-a6f1-95601fd92167","description":"Larry Ellison","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7f52-be7c-6459d2b77b3a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"On what date is Halloween?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"October 31 is All Hallows\' Eve, the evening before All Saints\' Day; Halloween comes from that older name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7378-9aed-70e760c248f9","description":"October 31","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7271-baa7-1d2ab3377581","description":"November 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-747f-afdb-27c226bf427e","description":"October 24","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7c97-9293-a8d8ee757c8c","description":"November 5","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-71ba-818a-54b620767df0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What do you call a business that lends and borrows money?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A bank often earns income by charging borrowers interest and may pay interest on customers\u2019 savings.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7e26-9a01-c5b3697621c3","description":"Bank","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7725-8fc2-43451745f8ea","description":"Book store","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-761c-92bb-8adca5845f2e","description":"Joint venture","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-71ae-8c34-d888866c7db3","description":"Pulp mill","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7543-9230-9383ab92b797","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the English title of the Christmas carol written by the Austrian Josef Mohr, originally called \'Stille Nacht\'?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Silent Night was first performed in 1818; Josef Mohr wrote the lyrics, and Franz Xaver Gruber composed the music.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7d3e-875b-ef4037319102","description":"Silent Night","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7170-bc25-12a8b05dd8b1","description":"The Holly and the Ivy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7c6e-98a5-2acf767623c1","description":"Oh, Holy Night","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-728f-8e5d-a92b92c4ed4d","description":"We Three Kings","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-771a-be7a-b19b8f8dc5c7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which toy is a multi-colored block you have to reorganize?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Rubik\'s Cube was created by Hungarian architect Ern\u0151 Rubik and was first called the Magic Cube.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-555c-79c0-b914-31db194875d7","description":"Rubik\'s Cube","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-76e1-aea7-83d181d46895","description":"Furby","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-7857-9e33-34bec6f11363","description":"Playmobil","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-555c-763b-a726-95a400